# Build artifacts (Rust & cargo)
# No tracked Cargo.lock (project rule) — see .claude/board/ISSUES.md
# ISS-STALE-AUTHORITY-LOCKS. A tracked Cargo.lock that pins the OGAR
# authority is a second, silently-stale reading of the codebook.
#
# Blanket, not per-path: the rule is "no locks ever", and a path list would
# have to grow on every new crate. The 27 crate-level locks this note once
# recorded as "still committed" were untracked on 2026-09-04 (`git rm --cached`)
# after the deferred pin sweep ran — see ISS-STALE-AUTHORITY-LOCKS-RESIDUE.
# Nothing under crates/ tracks a lock now, so the rule and the tree agree.
#
# Load-bearing, not cosmetic: release.yml regenerates the root lock
# (`cargo check`) and then runs `git add -A`, which would otherwise silently
# resurrect it on the next release.
Cargo.lock
/target/
/debug/
/release/
**/target/
**/debug/
**/release/
**/incremental/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
**/mutants.out*/

