# PROBE-CODEBOOK-44 real-data: Jina embeddings + vocab (derived data, license-unverified) — LOCAL ONLY
crates/bgz17/data/
crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/coca/*
!crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/coca/*.py
# Ignore the wordnet DATA, keep any GENERATOR (codebook must stay reproducible
# from the repo — data-in-Releases, code-in-repo).
crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/wordnet/*
!crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/wordnet/*.py
# PROIEL Greek NT treebank (CC BY-NC-SA — data stays local, never committed)
crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/proiel/
# German codebook from UD German-GSD/HDT (CC BY-SA — Release asset, not committed).
# Ignore the DATA (source .conllu + generated out/*.tsv), keep the GENERATOR: the
# codebook must stay reproducible from the repo (data-in-Releases, code-in-repo).
crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/de/*
!crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/de/build_de_codebook.py
# Rosetta probe data (PD Bible JSON lanes + generated out/) — data-in-Releases;
# keep the GENERATOR committed, ignore the data
crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/rosetta/*
!crates/lance-graph-planner/examples/data/rosetta/*.py

# ── REVERTED 2026-07-27: the plateau's branch-local generator ignore ──────
# A `**/*.py` / `**/*.sh` block here re-ignored (last-match-wins) the very
# generators the negations above deliberately track, and the plateau commit
# then swept all 11 off the branch — 5,790 lines of apparatus. That violated
# the rule written three times in THIS file: data-in-Releases, CODE-IN-REPO.
# Main was left holding the measurement receipts while the instruments that
# produced them lived on another branch. Reproducibility is not a per-PR
# size concern; the generators are permanent. Do not re-add such a block.

# Weather-probe fixtures — FETCHED, never committed (evaluation plan §0).
# 36 MB of ERA5 slabs; re-fetch with probes/weather-p1/fetch.py. The manifest
# IS committed as provenance (time_index / shape / nonfinite / min / max), so a
# fresh clone can verify which bytes a recorded result was produced from.
probes/weather-p1/fixture/**/*.npy
probes/weather-p1/fixture/*.npy
# Same rule, same reason, for D-WXS-7/D-WXS-8's fetch: the store's own
# .zmetadata (fetched fresh by fidelity_probe_fetch.py, 48 KB, deterministic
# from the public store) and the 138 MB of raw pair-distance f64 arrays
# fidelity_probe_prep.py writes. `fidelity_pairs/manifest.json` and the
# per-season `*_meta.txt` sidecars ARE committed (small, the provenance a
# fresh clone needs); `fidelity_probe_availability.json` and
# `fidelity_probe_results.json` ARE committed (the actual measured receipts).
# Re-derive the raw arrays with:
#   python3 probes/weather-p1/fidelity_probe_fetch.py
#   python3 probes/weather-p1/fidelity_probe_prep.py
probes/weather-p1/zmeta.json
probes/weather-p1/fixture/fidelity_pairs/*.f64
